// Failure golden: a literal column is declined by name, not dropped.
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)
//
// Three arm shapes that once declined now compile, because each needed only
// one arm body reached from more than one branch, and the compiler binds such
// a body once and lets each reaching branch force it: a top-level catch-all,
// an or-pattern with distinguishable alternatives, and two arms at one
// constructor head. `data-matched-arms.gandr` in the model tree is those three.
//
// A literal column is a DIFFERENT absence and no amount of sharing reaches it.
// `0` is not a constructor of any declared datatype, so there is no tag to
// place the arm at; deciding it needs an equality test the declared-data
// eliminator does not switch on. The arm is therefore declined by name.
//
// What this witness pins is that the decline stays a decline. A dropped arm
// would leave the item lowering cleanly and answering `1` for every `Some`,
// which is a wrong answer with no report; a declined arm leaves the item
// holey, so a goal is what a reader is given. The goal is the decline made
// observable, and its absence is the regression.
data Outer : Type {
  None : Outer;
  Some : (n : Integer) --> Outer;
}

def by_literal(m : Outer) -> F Integer {
  case m {
    Some(0) => ret 0,
    None => ret 1
  }
}

//@ expect: goal
